# Custom lib — app/src/lib/text.ts

## Context

`app/src/lib/text.ts` is a small in-house library with a fixed API. It is NOT
lodash/underscore, and agents tend to hallucinate helpers that don't exist. See
[materials/architecture-brief.md](../../materials/architecture-brief.md) (In-house library).

## Rule

- The entire supported API is exactly these three functions (import from `"./lib/text.js"` or a relative equivalent):
  - `slugify(input: string): string` — `"Buy Milk!"` → `"buy-milk"`
  - `truncate(input: string, maxLength: number, suffix = "…"): string` — result length includes the suffix
  - `normalizeSpaces(input: string): string` — `"  a   b "` → `"a b"`
- These helpers do NOT exist — never call them: `capitalize`, `camelCase`, `kebabCase`, `snakeCase`, `startCase`, `deburr`, `trim`, `pad`, `words`.
- If you need a new helper, add it explicitly to `app/src/lib/text.ts` as a named export with a colocated test in `app/src/lib/text.test.ts`; do not change the three existing signatures.
- NEVER import `lodash`, `lodash-es`, `lodash/*`, or `underscore`; use the functions above or plain `String` methods.

## How to verify

1. `git grep -n "^export function" -- app/src/lib/text.ts` — expect exactly the three signatures listed above (plus any explicitly added helpers).
2. `git grep -nwE "capitalize|camelCase|kebabCase|snakeCase|startCase|deburr" -- app/src ':!app/src/lib/text.ts'` — expect no matches.
3. `git grep -nE "from .(lodash|underscore)" -- app/src` — expect no matches.
4. `cd app; npm test` — `app/src/lib/text.test.ts` passes.
